description:
GitBak mirrors Bitbucket/GitHub/Gist repositories; paths, users,
and authentication are specified in ~/.gitbak.

When run, gitbak:

* asks for unspecified passwords;
* lists repositories using APIs - authenticating if necessary;
* clones/updates repositories;
* shows a summary (if verbose)

Gem created for comparing eLibri xml objects. More info coming soon. Currently working and tested only on REE.
Basic usage: Elibri::XmlVersions.new(product_ver1, product_ver2).diff
it will return hash: {:added => [], :changes => [], :deleted => []}

This gem provides two things;
One, a Register of elements in your app. These are concepts that you can discuss and make assertions about, such as a Carousel or a Search bar
Two, ElementProxies. These are created on demand, and provide helper functions on registered elements (such as carousel.visible or search.enter_text)

